<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10016" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντικέλευθος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pursuing an opposite path,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					4.74
				</span></i>
			; simply, <i>opposite,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					8.191
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καρκίνος ἀ. Αἰγοκερῆος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.658
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>opposing, hostile,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰχμή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.459
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				23.35
			</span></i>,al.</div>
